{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:stage1-recovery-codex-01\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result claims an occurrence rate for all 96 scheduled stations but divides the 18 observed occurrences by only the 72 stations retained after screening.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS as the selected result's exposure denominator even though the task and report define the target as the complete scheduled network.\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires one rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"observed_value\":\"complete scheduled network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The visible data include scheduled stations omitted by screening with unobserved occurrence flags, so the retained set is a strict subset of the scheduled domain.\",\"observed_value\":{\"scheduled\":true,\"screen_status\":\"omitted\",\"occurrence_flag\":\"NA\"},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report explicitly defines the target population as all 96 scheduled stations.\",\"observed_value\":96,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected report explicitly uses the 72 retained stations as its exposure denominator while labeling the resulting rate as applying to the entire scheduled network.\",\"observed_value\":{\"numerator\":18,\"denominator\":72,\"reported_rate\":0.25},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow constructs the same retained-subset denominator and complete-network claim directly.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS used as denominator\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"DENOMINATOR_LINE = f'Exposure denominator: the {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} stations retained after the signal screen.' + LF\\nSELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report transparently accounts for the full 96 stations, the 72 retained stations, the 24 omissions, and the retained-set numerator; this was considered as possible evidence that the intended estimand was conditional, but it does not change the explicitly complete-network target and claim.\",\"observed_value\":{\"scheduled\":96,\"retained\":72,\"omitted\":24,\"occurrences\":18},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled stations (planned units): 96\\nStations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"An approved deviation could potentially have altered the target or denominator, but the report states that none exists.\",\"observed_value\":false,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the mismatch by checking whether the scientific target or selected claim was explicitly conditional on passing the screen, or whether an approved deviation authorized that target change. The task and report instead specify the entire scheduled network, while the report states that no amendment or approved deviation exists; therefore the retained denominator cannot be reconciled with the declared complete-domain claim.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen.\",\"observed_value\":\"conditional on passing screen\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input semantics distinguish 72 signal-eligible assessed stations from 24 stations outside the eligible set and not assessed.\",\"observed_value\":{\"eligible\":72,\"outside_eligible\":24},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"accounting_group,station_count,occurrence_status\\nsignal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report defines the target as the 72 signal-eligible stations and reports the selected rate only among those stations.\",\"observed_value\":{\"numerator\":18,\"denominator\":72,\"rate\":\"25%\"},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow generates a conditional target and selected result using the same 72-station eligible domain.\",\"observed_value\":\"SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"TARGET_LINE = f'Target population: {SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.' + LF\\nACCOUNTING_LINE = f'Planned-unit accounting: {OCCURRENCES} eligible stations with an occurrence, {ELIGIBLE_WITHOUT_OCCURRENCE} eligible stations without an occurrence, and {OUTSIDE_ELIGIBLE} scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.' + LF\\nINPUT_LINE = f'Input table lines including header: {SOURCE_LINE_COUNT}.' + LF\\nRESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report also names a larger scheduled network of 96 stations, which was tested as possible evidence of a complete-domain target.\",\"observed_value\":96,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report accounts for 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set, but explicitly labels them outside the target set and not assessed rather than silently dropping them from a complete-domain claim.\",\"observed_value\":24,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the conditional interpretation by checking whether the mention of a 96-station scheduled network was used as the target or in a complete-network selected claim. It was not: both the stated target and selected result are expressly limited to the 72 signal-eligible stations, while the other 24 are identified as outside that eligible set.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The task requests a revised selected rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"observed_value\":\"entire scheduled survey network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The visible data show that omitted stations remain scheduled units even though their occurrence flags are unavailable.\",\"observed_value\":{\"scheduled\":true,\"screen_status\":\"omitted\",\"occurrence_flag\":\"NA\"},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected report retains all 96 scheduled stations in the exposure denominator and reports 18 divided by 96, not 18 divided by the 72 retained stations.\",\"observed_value\":{\"numerator\":18,\"denominator\":96,\"rate\":0.1875},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow constructs the selected result with SCHEDULED_STATIONS as the denominator.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"DENOMINATOR_LINE = f'Exposure denominator: all {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations, so the {OMITTED_STATIONS} omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.' + LF\\nSELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report explicitly characterizes the effect of unavailable observations as a lower-bound limitation and states that no screened-subset rate is reported.\",\"observed_value\":\"complete-domain lower bound\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":19,\"quoted_text\":\"The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The numerator is explicitly described as occurrences observed among only the retained stations, which was examined for a possible retained-subset rate.\",\"observed_value\":18,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations omitted by the signal screen and left without a usable observation: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow separately tracks 72 screen-passed stations, providing a possible route to the in-scope error, but the selected denominator line does not use that value.\",\"observed_value\":72,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\\nSCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\\nOMITTED_STATIONS = 24\\nOBSERVED_OCCURRENCES = 18\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the complete-domain denominator by checking whether the selected calculation used the available SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS value or reported 18/72. The selected report and generating workflow instead use all 96 scheduled stations, and the arithmetic is consistent because 18/96 = 0.1875. The unobserved outcomes and lower-bound interpretation may bear on other scientific questions, but they do not demonstrate the sole in-scope retained-subset-denominator issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}"}}
